# Web updates — Prompt & Services sync (mandatory)

Whenever the user asks to **update**, **add**, or **redesign** a web feature, Stock Calculator tab,
API job, or framework workflow, **in the same session** also update applicable entries in:

1. **Prompt tab** — `web/lib/agent/prompt-guidelines.ts` (`PROMPT_CATEGORIES`)
2. **Services tab** — `web/lib/services-catalog.ts` (`SERVICE_CATEGORIES`)

Do this **by default** without waiting for a separate request. Skip only when the change is
purely internal (CSS typo, refactor with no user-facing workflow change).

## When to add or edit

| Change type | Prompt tab | Services tab |
|-------------|------------|--------------|
| New Stock Calculator tab or major section | Copy-paste prompt for agent to populate StockBook + run analysis | Link to tab + refresh prompt if data-driven |
| New one-click API job (`/api/services/run`) | Optional companion prompt for manual/AI follow-up | `actionType: 'api'` entry + pack membership if daily |
| New copy-paste agent workflow | New `PromptExample` with framework refs | Mirror as `actionType: 'prompt'` if runnable from Services |
| Framework doc restructure (Part A/B, Gordon PE, etc.) | Update affected prompt text + `framework[]` tags | Update related service descriptions/prompts |
| Quarterly / news / morning run cascade | Update steps in post-results prompts | Update refresh-quarter-results and dependency descriptions |

## Quality bar

- Prompts must reference **StockBook paths**, framework files, and evidence labels (FACT / ASSUMPTION).
- Services must have **title**, **description**, **cadence**, **channel** (`web` | `cursor` | `both`).
- Use placeholders: `{TICKER}`, `{DATE}`, `{SECTOR}`, `{AMOUNT}` — document in `placeholders` on Prompt tab.
- Cross-link: Services panel links to `/chat/prompts`; keep IDs aligned where the same workflow appears in both.

## Files (do not duplicate elsewhere)

- Prompt UI: `web/components/PromptGuidelinesPanel.tsx` (reads `prompt-guidelines.ts`)
- Services UI: `web/components/ServicesPanel.tsx` (reads `services-catalog.ts`)

After edits, run `npm run build` in `web/` if TypeScript changed.
